From: Lumia 1520 mainline port <none@localhost>
Subject: [BACKPORT] regmap: slimbus: pass slim_device as the bus context

The regmap-slimbus bus callbacks take their context as a struct slim_device:

	static int regmap_slimbus_read(void *context, ...)
	{
		struct slim_device *sdev = context;

but this kernel passes something else in both paths.

__regmap_init_slimbus() passes &slimbus->dev. That happens to work only
because struct device dev is the first member of struct slim_device, so the
two addresses are numerically equal -- it is type confusion that survives by
layout accident.

__devm_regmap_init_slimbus() passes &slimbus, the address of the function's
own parameter. Once the function returns, every register access dereferences
a dead stack slot as if it were a slim_device.

Pass slimbus itself in both cases, which is what current upstream does. This
is a backport of that fix to the msm8974 tree, kept separate from any codec
work so it can be dropped once the tree catches up.
---
diff -urN orig/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c new/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c
--- a/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c	2026-07-30 18:37:15.541824579 -0400
+++ b/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c	2026-07-30 18:37:15.541875045 -0400
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(bus))
 		return ERR_CAST(bus);
 
-	return __regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, &slimbus->dev, config,
+	return __regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, slimbus, config,
 			     lock_key, lock_name);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__regmap_init_slimbus);
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(bus))
 		return ERR_CAST(bus);
 
-	return __devm_regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, &slimbus, config,
+	return __devm_regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, slimbus, config,
 				  lock_key, lock_name);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__devm_regmap_init_slimbus);
